  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9d52e811169e234b996c7a3d9272a3f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue: {fileID: 91567674}
  TextToBeShown:
  - Tunku at Year 1941-1945 did not have too many chances to show himself.
  - However, when that time, Tunku was still trying to stand against the Japanese.
  - After Japan surrended on August 1945
  - Malays at Kedah were parts of Malaya people wanting for independence.
  - On 10 October 1945, the Secretary of State for the Colonies issued his Policy
    Statement on the " Malayan Union ."
  - 'In Kedah, the two main Malay organisations held meetings and protest rallies. '
  - The Tunku spoke loudly at these rallies, but he suggested peaceful opposition.
  viewDistance: 7
