  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9d52e811169e234b996c7a3d9272a3f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue: {fileID: 91567674}
  TextToBeShown:
  - Malaya continued to be a British protectorate, while restoring the original symbolic
    status of the Malay rulers and tightening citizenship.
  - At this time, the British colonial government declared the Malayan Communist
    Party an illegal organization.
  - The relationship between the Malayan Communist Party and the British colonial
    government broke down completely, and turned to armed struggle.
  - the British colonists implemented the policy of "fortifying the walls and clearing
    the fields", and moved the Chinese who were originally scattered in the suburbs
    to designated locations with strict security, forming the later Kampung Baru
    Cina.
  viewDistance: 7
